Wi-Fi Security Protocols

These are different from Wi-Fi generations.

Security	Encryption	Security level	Notes
WEP	RC4	🔴 Broken	Never use
WPA	TKIP	🔴 Deprecated	Replacement for WEP
WPA2	AES/CCMP	🟡 Strong when configured correctly	Still widely used
WPA3	AES/CCMP/GCMP	🟢 Strongest modern standard	Recommended
WPA3-Enterprise	802.1X/EAP	🟢 Enterprise	Used by organizations

Wi-Fi Standard
     │
     ├── 802.11n → Wi-Fi 4
     ├── 802.11ac → Wi-Fi 5
     ├── 802.11ax → Wi-Fi 6
     └── 802.11be → Wi-Fi 7

Wi-Fi Security
     │
     ├── WEP
     ├── WPA
     ├── WPA2
     └── WPA3

Network Authentication
     │
     ├── WPA2-Personal
     │       └── PSK/password
     │
     └── WPA2/WPA3-Enterprise
             └── 802.1X / EAP

Wi-Fi itself operates primarily at Layers 1–2 of the TCP/IP model, while TCP and UDP operate at Layer 4 (Transport).

Application     HTTP / DNS / SSH
       ↓
Transport       TCP / UDP
       ↓
Internet        IPv4 / IPv6
       ↓
Network Access  Ethernet / Wi-Fi

This is the part that ties Wi-Fi → IP → TCP/UDP → ports → packets all together.
